## Part 1: Python Engine for Currency Rounding & Precision Flaws
Standard multi-threading scripts fail because they send requests sequentially, giving the database time to update your balance between threads. To find a hidden logic flaw, you must compress the requests into an HTTP/2 Single-Packet Attack. This script queues multiple requests and holds them at the server's gate, releasing them into the backend processing pipeline at the exact same microsecond.
## The Python Attack Script
